Step 7 of the build-up. Identical to linux-thread-vs-vcpu-thread-6.svg (see
that prompt), with nothing moved, plus a prominent mark on the first
kernel -> guest switch as the problem KVM solves:

- A bold red (#8a0404) arrow from the kernel bar down to the guest bar, drawn
  on top of the grey connector, framed by a red rounded ring (light red
  fill) around the switch.
- A thin red pointer from the ring down into the free area below the lanes,
  with a right-aligned red callout left of it: "KVM solves this problem:"
  (bold) / "context switch into the VM -" / "guest code runs on the real
  CPU".
- Keep the callout left of x ~ 560; steps 8 and 9 put their captions to the
  right of it.
